302	95,1170,612,2098 - 442,1725,615,2100 - 490,1655,615,1725 - 410,1788,442,1882	302. Piece of Side-flowering Sandwort.	A leafy stem with pairs of opposite, pointed, many-nerved leaves, and from a joint a slender branch bearing one small open five-petalled flower and a bud.
303	405,1660,772,2048 - 400,1655,480,1722 - 400,1722,440,1786 - 400,1884,446,2050 - 725,1880,775,2050	303. Flower magnified.	The same flower enlarged and seen from above: five rounded petals between pointed sepals, a ring of stamens, and the ovary with three styles at the centre.
304	728,1890,928,2035	304. A seed divided, showing the embryo coiled around the outside of the albumen.	A kidney-shaped seed cut in half, the curved embryo lying like a band round the outside of the shaded albumen.
305	728,1175,928,1578	305. Pistil of Sand-Spurrey cut through lengthwise and magnified.	A long oval ovary split lengthwise, its seeds hanging in rows from a central column, with slender hairy styles rising from the top.
306	1062,1425,1198,1588	306. Lower part of the ovary of the same, cut across.	The base of the ovary sliced across, showing a ring of seeds around the central column in a single cell.
307	1358,1460,1598,2102	307. Flower of a Catchfly cut through lengthwise.	A long tubular calyx cut open lengthwise, showing the ovary on its stalk inside, with stamens and narrow-clawed petals rising above.
308	1032,1665,1302,2102	308. A separate petal.	One petal of the Catchfly: a long narrow claw widening into a fan-shaped blade with a small scale where the two meet.
